 r'Put \(\theta_i=(i-\tfrac12)\pi/d\), \(t_i=(1,\sqrt2\cos\theta_i,\ldots,\sqrt2\cos(q\theta_i))\), and \(L=2r+3\log(1000d)\). Source index \(i\) corresponds to Lean index \(i.val+1\).',
 r'Define \(Y_i=d^{-1}(\Phi_i\Phi_i^\top\otimes t_it_i^\top)\mathbf1_{\{\|\Phi_i\|^2\le L\}}\), \(M_i=\int Y_i\,d\mu\), and \(Z_i=Y_i-M_i\). The cutoff is closed and specific to row \(i\); all integrals use the same original unconditional \(\mu\).',
 r'Matrices have the standard finite-coordinate Borel structure and real Euclidean operator norm topology. The local Lean measurable-space definition fixes this standard structure; it is not a caller-supplied assumption.',
